.TITLE "winget"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
winget is a tool that lets you **install and update software** using your terminal.

It was created by __Microsoft__ to make managing apps easier.
You can think of it like a personal assistant for your computer. 
Instead of searching the web for a download button, you just **ask winget to get it** for you.

.DIV "EXAMPLE"
winget search vscode

.DIV "EXPLANATION"
**winget search** looks for the app you want to install.

Here, __winget__ is the name of the tool.
__search__ is the action that scans the available apps.
__vscode__ is an example of what you might be looking for.

This helps you **find the exact name** of the software before you download it.

.DIV "EXAMPLE"
winget install vscode

.DIV "EXPLANATION"
**winget install** gets the app and sets it up on your computer.

Here, __install__ is the command that **does all the work**.

This is much safer than downloading files from the web, as it **skips the manual setup** windows.

.DIV "EXAMPLE"
winget upgrade --all

.DIV "EXPLANATION"
**winget upgrade --all** brings all your apps up to the latest version.

Here, __upgrade__ tells the tool to check for newer versions.
__--all__ is a flag that tells it to **update everything it finds**.

This is the easiest way to **keep your software current** and running smoothly.

.DIV "SUMMARY"
winget takes the stress out of managing software on Windows.
Try running **winget upgrade --all** once a week to **keep your system fresh** and secure.
